---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: >-
  The spikes of one plan, as a plan graph: the writer of the brief of what they will
  measure, and the spikes the draft adds, which run beside it and never wait on it. The
  draft creates it as `<plan>-spikes` only when the plan needs a measurement; the planning
  run's `spikes` step launches it in the same flow, and its `finalize` step reworks the
  plan from their reports. Finalize is
  not a member here because the engine refuses any node depending on a `publish:
  "preserve"` node, and every spike is one.
variables:
  plan:
    description: The qualified id of the plan whose spikes these are, `authoring:<native id>`.
    type: text
    required: true
  native:
    description: The plan project's native id.
    type: text
    required: true
members:
  - id: "{{ native }}-spikes-brief"
    title: "Write the spike brief of {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: spike-brief.md.j2}
    answers:
      plan: "{{ plan }}"
      native: "{{ native }}"
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: spike-brief
      onepipeline.persona: ../personas/spike-brief.yaml
      onepipeline.agent_graph: graphs/spike-brief.yaml
---
The spikes of `{{ plan }}`: the spike brief's writer and each spike, run side by side.
